  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway where Dianversicoside G may influence VMRC-MELG through a series of intermediate targets. Specifically, Dianversicoside G is linked to Hepatocyte, which is a target of both Propenyl propyl disulfide and 5-Propyloxolan-2-One. These compounds, in turn, target VMRC-MELG. This suggests that Dianversicoside G may exert its effects via a metabolic or enzymatic cascade that ultimately leads to the activation of VMRC-MELG. The shared involvement of Hepatocyte and the common target of both Propenyl propyl disulfide and 5-Propyloxolan-2-One further supports a possible mechanism involving cellular metabolism or signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, mechanism by which Dianversicoside G may interact with VMRC-MELG.",
